        "subject": "LU-20579 tests: use ip(8) for the test_109 interface alias",
        "message": "LU-20579 tests: use ip(8) for the test_109 interface alias\n\ntest_109 added and removed the alias with ifconfig, which comes\nfrom the deprecated net-tools package and is absent on minimal\nRHEL 9 images. The test failed at setup on such nodes.\n\nUse ip(8), as setup_fakeif() in the same test already does. These\nwere the only two ifconfig calls in the suite. The alias address\nnow carries an explicit /31, matching FAKE_IP, in place of the\nclassful /8 that ifconfig applied to a 10.x address.\n\nDrop the paired address delete. cleanup_fakeif() removes the veth\npair on the next line and takes the alias with it. The delete was\nfatal, so a stale address turned an otherwise passed test into a\nfailure and skipped the remaining teardown.\n\nFixes: 7dcdb9eb0ded (\"LU-16859 lnet: incorrect check for duplicate NI\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: Ib7b4eb5cd91bf6a80187259d77d4f37857212dd9\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67931\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
